  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer planar dielectric stack on silicon substrate with air incidence using HfO2 and SiO2 in alternating sequence. Initialize layer thicknesses using stratified sampling with ±15% variance around theoretical quarter-wave optical thicknesses calculated at 8000nm and 13000nm band edges. Impose hard upper bound of 2000nm on each individual layer thickness during optimization. Target high emissivity (absorptance) in 8000-13000nm wavelength band and low emissivity in 3000-5000nm band. Use differential evolution or gradient-based optimizer with Transfer Matrix Method evaluation. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm array. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3000-5000 nm, 8000-13000 nm. soft objectives: high emissivity in 8000-13000 nm; low emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 24.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize 24 alternating HfO2 and SiO2 planar layers on a silicon substrate with air incidence. Initialize thicknesses near quarter-wave optical depths at 8000 nm and 13000 nm with ±15% variance, enforcing a hard 2000 nm upper bound per layer. Maximize average emissivity (absorptance) in 8000–13000 nm while minimizing average emissivity in 3000–5000 nm over normal unpolarized illumination using a gradient-based optimizer coupled with Transfer Matrix Method evaluation.",
